VALUES (635, '1', $t$ASK 635: hydrogen's output-token limit is raised from 65,536 to 131,072$t$,
  $t$Give hydrogen enough output room that, after its reasoning, it can still write the judgment. In run 42517 hydrogen, as a panel judge, used 65,536 of 65,536 output tokens, 65,533 of them on reasoning, finished "length" and returned no text. Expected effect: when hydrogen judges, the reply ends "stop" with judgment text. Not promised: the record cannot show that 131,072 is enough; hydrogen has filled every limit it was given as a judge. No reasoning setting is touched. (plan rev 1, heading 1, ask635/w4/plan635.md md5 a9fa07cf)$t$,
  'not yet',
  $t$Written by W4 at 05:14 CST 2026-11-25 on the operator's press "Write it" on W4's card (written, Wall 11971; audit 42082), and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11975). One value in one row: model_config seat hydrogen (google/gemini-4-hydrogen) max_tokens 65,536 to 131,072, guarded on the prior value; a note line holds the undo value 65536. No engine or child node, no reasoning, temperature or model id, and no other seat changed. NOT YET, because the objective is hydrogen returning a verdict as a judge and no run has been made since the write. W4's search (plan heading 3): Resolve Seats and Panel Build pass max_tokens to the request with floors and no cap; the judge call's timeout is 900 s and the engine stops waiting at 980 s. W4's measure from one call: 65,536 tokens took about 343 s in run 42517, so a full 131,072 would take about 690 s, a guess against a 900 s timeout; a full judge call at the new limit costs about 1.10 dollars. The three legitimate results on a run where hydrogen judges (plan C3): (a) the reply ends "stop" with a stored judgment; (b) the ASK 629 line "returned no text: finish_reason length; output tokens 131,072", which means 131,072 is not enough; (c) a time-out, which means the limit is too high for the time allowed. (b) and (c) go back to the operator. W1's notes on the plan (Wall 11960): N1 Panel Judges Parallel has a 60 s timeout (it only dispatches); N2 the criteria should name the time-out outcome; N3 the operator's quotation was not checked by W1. Plan criterion C2 (an offline replay of Resolve Seats and Panel Build with the new row) was to run before the card and was SKIPPED, W4's stated mistake (Wall 11980); W4 ran it after the write, at 05:25 CST 2026-11-25: 5 PASS, 0 FAIL, the live Resolve Seats on the 42517 inputs gives the hydrogen judge 131,072 and nothing else in its output changes; Panel Build was checked from its code, not replayed. W1 reproduced it, 5 PASS with identical output (Wall 11982). NOT SEARCHED by W4: OpenRouter's per-provider endpoint limits. Open: two clean live runs in which hydrogen judges. REVISION (this row): the engine manual is WRITTEN, part 10.0 v311 to v321 (438a0c8d, 63,057 characters), on the operator's press "Write it" at 05:47 CST 2026-11-25 on W3's card, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11983, 11984). objective_met stays 'not yet'. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). NOT EXERCISED. Hydrogen did not judge (the JUDGE ORDER line: "LEFT OUT: ... hydrogen (is a debater)"). As the Oracle its output per call was 20,042 (D1), 33,534 (D2), 57,655 (D3), 38,961 (D3B), 31,344 (D4) and 59,476 (D4B), each under the old limit of 65,536, so the raised limit was never needed. The row's line "SYNTHESIS USAGE: prompt=97624 completion=29454 reasoning=24432 finish=stop max_tokens=131072" is the qwen/qwen4-max call (call_costs "Synthesis Call openrouter", output 29,454) and shows nothing of this ASK. ERROR on the record: W4's review (Wall 12772) and the report's first text read that line as this ASK passing; corrected on Wall 12800. RELATED DEFECT, outside this ASK: the question-round answer call does not use this limit; it is sent with a fixed 4,000, and hydrogen's third answer ended there with no text (ASK 674, planned). W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
  '11959, 11960, 11971, 11975, 11954, 11974, 11976, 11977, 11980, 11982, 11983, 11984, 12787, 12791, 12797, 12799, 12800, 12802, 12803, 12804, 12789',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), 225,
  to_jsonb($t$(1) Project chat, 04:41 CST 2026-11-25 (message cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo589SHYu1ca6GGbyLrQ8xVXBq): "let's increase hydrogen tokens." The same message answered 630, 631 and 624 (Wall 11954). (2) W4's write card (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58KVszvhk32wAUdh8kGQne16, "Raise hydrogen's output limit from 65,536 to 131,072 tokens?"): he pressed "Write it" at 05:14 CST 2026-11-25. The card is from W4's thread note to W3 of 05:19 CST; W3 did not read it. There was no build card: nothing was built.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "source": "W4's thread note to W3, 05:19 CST 2026-11-25; Wall 11971; audit 42082. Card not read by W3.", "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58KVszvhk32wAUdh8kGQne16", "question": "Raise hydrogen's output limit from 65,536 to 131,072 tokens?", "press_time": "05:14 CST 2026-11-25", "instruction": {"time": "04:41 CST 2026-11-25", "where": "project chat", "words": "let's increase hydrogen tokens.", "message_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo589SHYu1ca6GGbyLrQ8xVXBq"}}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "a9fa07cf", "note": "plan rev 1; rev 0 (803c9032, commit a7c022ab) graded PASS WITH N1 to N3 by W1 (Wall 11960, commit 28082b0c); rev 1 applies them by its own first line. No Wall grade of rev 1 by itself was found by W3.", "path": "ask635/w4/plan635.md", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11959, 11960"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[]$j$::jsonb,
